<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    The plans of release E's peoples' towns (docs/design/peoples.md, "Release E"; the format is in Rimfolk_TownPlans.xml's
    header; Source/ColonyCouncil/Peoples/PeopleTowns.cs places them). Only the base game's buildings, so every plan stands
    without the DLCs; the tests check every plan (Tools/Tests/PeoplesTests.cs). Each tells its people's story: the
    Stormglass Conclave's glass tower of records with rods round its rim and a weather garden, the Mossborn's houses and
    seed vault among the trees with their burial grove of saplings, the Ashen Banner's walled barracks fort with its drill
    yard and the hall of the Roll, the Kiln Guild's carved guildhall beside its kilns and a market of masterworks.
  -->

  <ColonyCouncil.TownPlanDef>
    <defName>Rimfolk_Plan_GlassTower</defName>
    <label>glass tower</label>
    <description>The Stormglass Conclave's tower: the reading hall of the storm records in marble, shelves of the record along its north wall, the readers' benches and a long table, a house of beds and a storehouse beside it, a weather garden of roses and daylilies on flagstones round a fire, and lightning rods of steel standing round the whole of it.</description>
